{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771234151293,"sessionID":"ses_39a387835ffeQXkadxFvThlMO2","part":{"id":"prt_c65c84b71001m1dgwILGfC2tZz","sessionID":"ses_39a387835ffeQXkadxFvThlMO2","messageID":"msg_c65c81ebc0014HhL2YK11171H8","type":"tool","callID":"call_0b2e792629274854be706fd0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","offset":1130},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1130: - Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n1131: - Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n1132: - All 341 tests passing\n1133: \n1134: **Technical Decisions:**\n1135: \n1136: - Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n1137: - Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n1138: - Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n1139: - Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n1140: - Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n1141: - Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n1142: - Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n1143: \n1144: **Test Coverage:**\n1145: \n1146: - All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n1147: - Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n1148: - Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n1149: \n1150: **Implementation Summary (Export/Import JSON):**\n1151: \n1152: - Implemented Export JSON button in SettingsPanel footer\n1153: - Implemented Import JSON button with hidden file input\n1154: - Export creates downloadable JSON file (gol-expert-settings.json)\n1155: - Import loads JSON file with validation\n1156: - Comprehensive validation for all expert settings parameters\n1157: - Error message display for invalid imports\n1158: - File format: JSON with pretty-printing (2-space indentation)\n1159: - Blob-based file download with URL.createObjectURL\n1160: - FileReader API for file upload\n1161: - All 349 tests passing\n1162: \n1163: **Technical Decisions:**\n1164: \n1165: - Export uses Blob and URL.createObjectURL for download\n1166: - Pretty-printed JSON with 2-space indentation\n1167: - Import validates against all parameter ranges\n1168: - Custom validation function returns detailed error messages\n1169: - Hidden file input triggered via button click\n1170: - Error state managed in component state\n1171: - Invalid settings prevent import with user feedback\n1172: \n1173: **Validation Coverage:**\n1174: \n1175: - Movement detection: centroidHistoryLength (3-10), movementThreshold (0.1-2.0), minClusterSize (1-5)\n1176: - Scoring: moverPointsPerGeneration (1-100), oscillatorPointsPerGeneration (0-20), scoreMultiplier (0.1-5.0)\n1177: - Level generation: baseTimeSeconds (10-120), timeIncrementPerLevel (0-60), baseFlux (5-50), difficultyScalingMode (TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME)\n1178: - Grid sizing: mobileCellSize (14-24), desktopCellSize (16-28), minVisibleCells (≥1)\n1179: - Audio: enabled (boolean), volume (0-0.5), waveform (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n1180: \n1181: **Test Coverage:**\n1182: \n1183: - All existing 349 tests continue to pass\n1184: - Export functionality verified through manual testing\n1185: - Import functionality verified with valid and invalid JSON files\n1186: - Error handling tested for malformed JSON\n1187: \n1188: ### 5.2 Presets System (LOW - Convenience)\n1189: \n1190: - [x] Implement preset configurations\n1191:   - Easy: Lower difficulty, generous resources\n1192:   - Normal: Balanced gameplay\n1193:   - Hard: Strict time/flux limits\n1194:   - Chaos: Extreme parameters, unpredictable\n1195: - [x] Implement preset selection UI\n1196:   - Dropdown in Expert Settings\n1197:   - Preview preset values\n1198: - [ ] Add custom preset support\n1199:   - Allow users to save current settings as preset\n1200:   - Name and save custom configurations\n1201:   - NOT YET IMPLEMENTED\n1202: \n1203: **Dependencies**: Expert settings\n1204: \n1205: **Implementation Summary:**\n1206: \n1207: - Implemented Preset type in src/types/index.ts with four preset options: EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS\n1208: - Implemented src/lib/presets.ts library with applyPreset(), getPresetDescription(), and preset configurations\n1209: - Created four preset configurations with balanced parameter sets:\n1210:   - EASY: Generous Flux (30), longer time limits (90s), lenient scoring (15pt movers, 3pt oscillators), lower movement threshold (0.3)\n1211:   - NORMAL: Balanced Flux (20), standard time limits (60s), standard scoring (10pt movers, 2pt oscillators), standard movement threshold (0.5)\n1212:   - HARD: Limited Flux (15), shorter time limits (40s), strict scoring (8pt movers, 1pt oscillators), higher movement threshold (0.7)\n1213:   - CHAOS: Extreme Flux (10), very short time limits (30s), chaotic scoring (5pt movers, 1pt oscillators), low movement threshold (0.1), larger grid sizing (28px desktop, 22px mobile)\n1214: - Updated SettingsPanel.tsx to include preset selector with description at top of panel\n1215: - Updated SettingsPanel.css with preset section styling\n1216: - Updated createInitialExpertSettings() in src/lib/state.ts to use NORMAL preset by default\n1217: - Added comprehensive test suite with 11 tests covering all presets and edge cases\n1218: - All tests passing (360 total)\n1219: \n1220: **Technical Decisions:**\n1221: \n1222: - Preset type defined as enum-like string union: 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'\n1223: - applyPreset() performs deep clone using JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) to prevent mutation issues\n1224: - getPresetDescription() returns human-readable description for each preset explaining the balance and intended difficulty\n1225: - Preset selector placed at top of SettingsPanel for easy access and visibility\n1226: - Preset descriptions use glassmorphism styling with subtle background for readability\n1227: - Default preset is NORMAL for balanced gameplay experience\n1228: - All preset parameters validated against spec-defined ranges\n1229: - Preset application immediately updates all expert settings without requiring panel close/reopen\n1230: - Preset configurations include all expert settings: movement detection, scoring, level generation, grid sizing, and audio parameters\n1231: \n1232: **Test Coverage: 11 tests**\n1233: \n1234: - Preset type definition: 1 test\n1235: - EASY preset configuration: 1 test\n1236: - NORMAL preset configuration: 1 test\n1237: - HARD preset configuration: 1 test\n1238: - CHAOS preset configuration: 1 test\n1239: - applyPreset() deep clone behavior: 1 test\n1240: - applyPreset() applies correct values: 1 test\n1241: - getPresetDescription() returns correct descriptions: 3 tests (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS)\n1242: - Invalid preset handling: 1 test\n1243: \n1244: **Integration Notes:**\n1245: \n1246: - Presets integrated into SettingsPanel as dropdown selector at top of panel\n1247: - Preset selector onChange handler calls applyPreset() to update expert settings\n1248: - Preset descriptions displayed below selector to explain each preset's characteristics\n1249: - createInitialExpertSettings() now uses applyPreset('NORMAL') for default configuration\n1250: - Preset system works seamlessly with existing settings persistence (localStorage)\n1251: - Users can manually tweak parameters after selecting a preset for further customization\n1252: - Total test count: 360 tests passing (up from 349)\n1253: \n1254: **Implementation Summary (Tooltips/Documentation & Danger Zone):**\n1255: \n1256: - Added comprehensive help text for all expert settings parameters\n1257: - Each setting now has italicized help text explaining its purpose and valid range\n1258: - Added danger zone section at bottom of settings panel with red warning theme\n1259: - Implemented Chaos Multiplier control (0.5-10.0x) for scoring difficulty scaling\n1260: - Implemented Timer Speed control (0.5-5.0x) for level time countdown speed\n1261: - Updated ExpertSettings type to include optional chaosMultiplier and timerSpeed fields\n1262: - Updated all preset configurations (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS) with danger zone defaults\n1263: - Added validation for danger zone parameters in both SettingsPanel.tsx and settings.ts\n1264: - Added CSS styling for danger zone with warning banner and red-themed controls\n1265: - All 360 tests passing\n1266: \n1267: **Technical Decisions:**\n1268: \n1269: - Help text uses italicized styling with reduced opacity for subtle readability\n1270: - Danger zone placed at bottom of settings panel with distinct visual styling\n1271: - Red border and warning banner signal extreme/dangerous settings\n1272: - Danger zone controls use red-themed slider thumbs for visual distinction\n1273: - Defaults: chaosMultiplier=1.0, timerSpeed=1.0 for balanced gameplay\n1274: - Preset danger zone values: EASY (0.5x, 0.8x), NORMAL (1.0x, 1.0x), HARD (1.5x, 1.5x), CHAOS (3.0x, 2.5x)\n1275: - Optional fields in ExpertSettings type (chaosMultiplier?, timerSpeed?) for backward compatibility\n1276: - Validation prevents extreme values: chaosMultiplier (0.5-10.0), timerSpeed (0.5-5.0)\n1277: \n1278: **Test Coverage:**\n1279: \n1280: - All existing 360 tests continue to pass\n1281: - Preset tests updated to include new danger zone fields\n1282: - Settings validation tests include danger zone parameter checks\n1283: - Integration verified through manual testing\n1284: \n1285: **Implementation Notes:**\n1286: \n1287: - Danger zone settings allow experienced players to customize extreme game modes\n1288: - Help text makes expert settings more accessible to new players\n1289: - Visual hierarchy separates normal settings from dangerous ones\n1290: - Changes propagate through existing preset and settings persistence systems\n1291: \n1292: ---\n1293: \n1294: ## Sprint 6: Quality Assurance\n1295: \n1296: _Goal: Stability, accessibility, and performance_\n1297: \n1298: ### 6.1 Error Handling & Resilience (MEDIUM - Stability)\n1299: \n1300: - [x] Implement global error boundary (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1301:   - Catch React component errors\n1302:   - Display user-friendly error message\n1303:   - Log error details\n1304: - [x] Add input validation\n1305:   - Validate all user inputs\n1306:   - Validate configuration parameters\n1307:   - Prevent NaN and infinity\n1308: - [x] Handle edge cases gracefully\n1309:   - Empty grid states\n1310:   - Zero flux scenarios\n1311:   - Invalid level numbers\n1312:   - Corrupted localStorage\n1313: - [ ] Add retry mechanisms\n1314:   - Retry failed operations with exponential backoff\n1315:   - Graceful degradation when features fail\n1316: - [x] Handle browser compatibility\n1317:   - Check for required APIs (Web Audio, Canvas)\n1318:   - Fallbacks for unsupported features\n1319:   - Clear error messages\n1320: \n1321: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1322: \n1323: **Implementation Summary (Browser Compatibility & Edge Case Handling):**\n1324: \n1325: - Created centralized feature detection module (src/lib/featureDetection.ts) with checks for:\n1326:   - Web Audio API (AudioContext/webkitAudioContext)\n1327:   - Canvas API (canvas.getContext('2d'))\n1328:   - localStorage availability\n1329:   - requestAnimationFrame support\n1330:   - performance.now() support\n1331:   - devicePixelRatio support\n1332:   - Page Visibility API support\n1333:   - Touch events support\n1334: - Enhanced localStorage handling (src/lib/state.ts) with:\n1335:   - QuotaExceededError handling with automatic cleanup\n1336:   - cleanupOldLocalStorageData() function to free space\n1337:   - Enhanced loadFromLocalStorage() with optional validator parameter\n1338:   - isLocalStorageAvailable() function for storage checks\n1339: - Integrated feature detection into main.tsx with logUnsupportedFeatures() call on app initialization\n1340: - Added comprehensive test coverage for feature detection (10 tests)\n1341: - All existing 364 tests continue to pass (374 total with new tests)\n1342: \n1343: **Technical Decisions:**\n1344: \n1345: - Feature detection runs at module load time for early detection of unsupported features\n1346: - localStorage quota exceeded triggers cleanup of all game data, then retries save\n1347: - Validation function parameter allows type-safe data loading from localStorage\n1348: - Logger integration for warning about unsupported features\n1349: - isBrowserSupported() checks critical features: canvas, requestAnimationFrame, localStorage\n1350: - Cleanup function removes all keys with 'gol-' prefix to prevent orphaned data\n1351: \n1352: **Test Coverage: 10 tests (new)**\n1353: \n1354: - features object structure and types\n1355: - Audio, Canvas, localStorage detection functions\n1356: - logUnsupportedFeatures() function\n1357: - getFeatureSupport() function\n1358: - isBrowserSupported() function\n1359: \n1360: **Total: 374 tests passing (up from 364)**\n1361: \n1362: **Implementation Summary (Error Boundary):**\n1363: \n1364: - Implemented ErrorBoundary class component in src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx with comprehensive error handling\n1365: - Implemented getDerivedStateFromError lifecycle method to catch React errors and set error state\n1366: - Implemented componentDidCatch lifecycle method to log error details to console\n1367: - Implemented user-friendly error UI with \"Something went wrong\" message and reload button\n1368: - Implemented development-only error details section showing error message, component stack, and stack trace\n1369: - Created ErrorBoundary.css with glassmorphism styling matching application theme\n1370: - Added ErrorBoundary.test.tsx with 4 comprehensive tests covering all error scenarios\n1371: - Integrated ErrorBoundary into App.tsx to wrap all application components\n1372: - Error boundary displays reload button that refreshes the page to recover from errors\n1373: \n1374: **Technical Decisions:**\n1375: \n1376: - Used class component (instead of function component) to implement getDerivedStateFromError lifecycle method\n1377: - Error details only shown in development mode (import.meta.env.DEV) for security\n1378: - Reload button uses window.location.reload() to fully refresh the application state\n1379: - Console.error called with both error object and component stack for debugging\n1380: - Glassmorphism design matches other UI components for consistent look and feel\n1381: - Error boundary positioned with z-index: 999999 to overlay all content\n1382: \n1383: **Test Coverage: 4 tests**\n1384: \n1385: - ErrorBoundary renders children when no error occurs\n1386: - ErrorBoundary catches errors and displays error UI\n1387: - ErrorBoundary logs error and component stack to console\n1388: - ErrorBoundary reload button is clickable and displayed\n1389: \n1390: **Integration Notes:**\n1391: \n1392: - ErrorBoundary wraps entire App component to catch all React errors\n1393: - All 364 tests passing (including 4 new ErrorBoundary tests)\n1394: - Error boundary prevents white screen crashes by providing user-friendly error UI\n1395: - Development mode shows detailed error information for debugging\n1396: - Production mode shows simplified error message for better user experience\n1397: \n1398: ### 6.2 Accessibility (LOW - Inclusivity)\n1399: \n1400: - [ ] Implement keyboard navigation\n1401:   - Arrow keys for grid navigation\n1402:   - Enter/Space to place cells\n1403:   - Escape to cancel/close panels\n1404:   - Tab navigation through UI controls\n1405: - [x] Add screen reader support (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1406:   - ARIA labels for UI elements\n1407:   - Announce game state changes\n1408:   - Alternative text for visual elements\n1409:   - Live regions for score/timer updates\n1410: - [x] Implement reduced motion support\n1411:   - Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query\n1412:   - Disable animations when requested\n1413:   - Simplified visual feedback\n1414: - [ ] Add high contrast mode\n1415:   - Toggle for high contrast colors\n1416:   - Larger text option\n1417:   - Improved readability\n1418: - [x] Ensure minimum touch targets\n1419:   - 44×44px minimum for mobile\n1420:   - Spacious clickable areas\n1421: - [ ] Focus management\n1422:   - Visible focus indicators\n1423:   - Logical tab order\n1424:   - Focus trap in modals\n1425: \n1426: **Dependencies**: UI components, user interaction\n1427: \n1428: **Implementation Summary (Screen Reader Support - 2026-02-16):**\n1429: \n1430: - Added ARIA labels to all buttons in GlassHUD (STEP, START/RUNNING, RANDOM, CLEAR, DRAW, ERASE, Small/Medium/Large, Show/Hide Grid, Settings)\n1431: - Added aria-pressed to toggle buttons (DRAW/ERASE modes, grid size presets, Show/Hide Grid)\n1432: - Added aria-live=\"polite\" regions to ScoreDisplay, FluxDisplay, and GlassHUD status items\n1433: - Added aria-label to score and high score displays with descriptive text\n1434: - Added aria-label to FluxDisplay with available flux information\n1435: - Added aria-label to IntroOverlay, VictoryScreen, ErrorBoundary buttons\n1436: - Added role=\"alert\" and aria-live=\"assertive\" to ErrorBoundary for error announcements\n1437: - Added role=\"dialog\" and aria-modal=\"true\" to SettingsPanel\n1438: - Added role=\"img\" and dynamic aria-label to Canvas element describing alive cell count\n1439: - Created Announcer component with sr-only class for screen reader announcements\n1440: - Integrated Announcer into Game component with phase-based announcements:\n1441:   - Planning phase: Announces level number and instructions\n1442:   - Countdown phase: Announces simulation starting soon\n1443:   - Running phase: Announces simulation progress and remaining time\n1444:   - Finished phase: Announces level completion\n1445:   - Level transition: Announces level completion with score and next level\n1446:   - Victory: Announces completion of all levels with total score\n1447: - Added .sr-only CSS class to index.css for visually hidden but accessible content\n1448: - All 374 tests passing with accessibility improvements\n1449: \n1450: **Technical Decisions:**\n1451: \n1452: - aria-live=\"polite\" for dynamic content to avoid interrupting users\n1453: - aria-live=\"assertive\" for error announcements to get immediate attention\n1454: - aria-atomic=\"true\" to announce complete messages\n1455: - role=\"status\" for dynamic game information updates\n1456: - .sr-only class uses standard accessible hiding technique (position absolute, 1px size, clip rect)\n1457: - Announcer component uses separate state to avoid re-render issues\n1458: - Phase-based announcements triggered on phase state changes\n1459: - Level completion announcements integrated into handleTransitionComplete callback\n1460: \n1461: **Implementation Summary (Reduced Motion Support):**\n1462: \n1463: - Added @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) queries to all 10 CSS files\n1464: - Disabled all animations (keyframe animations, transition properties, transform animations) when reduced motion is preferred\n1465: - Covered 76 animation/transition instances across entire codebase\n1466: - Files updated: VictoryScreen.css, IntroOverlay.css, TransitionOverlay.css, SettingsPanel.css, GlassHUD.css, ScoreDisplay.css, LevelStats.css, FluxDisplay.css, index.css, ErrorBoundary.css\n1467: - Prioritized disabling infinite animations (glitch, pulse-glow, pulse) as they cause most vestibular issues\n1468: - Simplified visual feedback for users with motion sensitivity by removing all motion\n1469: - All 364 tests passing with reduced motion support enabled\n1470: \n1471: **Technical Decisions:**\n1472: \n1473: - Used CSS @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) query to detect user's motion preference\n1474: - Set animation: none and transition: none for all animated elements when reduced motion is preferred\n1475: - Set transform: none for hover/active states to prevent scale animations\n1476: - Applied overrides at end of each CSS file to ensure they take precedence\n1477: - Maintains full functionality while removing all motion effects\n1478: - Respects OS-level accessibility settings for users with vestibular disorders or motion sensitivity\n1479: \n1480: ### 6.3 Performance Optimization (LOW - Performance)\n1481: \n1482: - [ ] Implement performance monitoring\n1483:   - FPS counter (development only)\n1484:   - Memory usage tracking\n1485:   - Component render profiling\n1486: - [ ] Add performance optimizations\n1487:   - Memoize expensive calculations\n1488:   - Virtualize large lists (if applicable)\n1489:   - Lazy load non-critical components\n1490:   - Debounce/throttle frequent operations\n1491: - [ ] Profile and optimize\n1492:   - Identify performance bottlenecks\n1493:   - Optimize critical paths\n1494:   - Ensure 60fps with 500+ cells\n1495:   - Test on low-end devices\n1496: - [ ] Implement lazy loading\n1497:   - Load audio on first interaction\n1498:   - Lazy load expert settings panel\n1499:   - Code splitting for production\n1500: \n1501: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1502: \n1503: ### 6.4 Testing (LOW - Quality Assurance)\n1504: \n1505: - [ ] Set up testing framework\n1506:   - Choose testing framework (Vitest recommended)\n1507:   - Configure test environment\n1508:   - Set up coverage reporting\n1509: - [ ] Write unit tests for simulation engine\n1510:   - Rule application (born/survive)\n1511:   - Toroidal boundaries\n1512:   - Age tracking\n1513:   - Edge cases (empty grid, static patterns)\n1514: - [ ] Write unit tests for phase management\n1515:   - Phase transitions\n1516:   - Guard conditions\n1517:   - Timer accuracy\n1518: - [ ] Write unit tests for flux management\n1519:   - Placement and refund logic\n1520:   - Phase-based behavior\n1521: - [ ] Write unit tests for movement detection\n1522:   - Connected component detection\n1523:   - Centroid tracking\n1524:   - Classification accuracy\n1525: - [ ] Write unit tests for scoring system\n1526:   - Score calculation accuracy\n1527:   - Score cap handling\n1528:   - High score persistence\n1529: - [ ] Write unit tests for level progression\n1530:   - Level configuration generation\n1531:   - Difficulty scaling\n1532: - [ ] Write integration tests\n1533:   - End-to-end game flow\n1534:   - Level progression\n1535:   - Score calculation\n1536:   - UI interaction\n1537: - [ ] Add manual testing procedures\n1538:   - Mobile responsiveness\n1539:   - Touch interaction\n1540:   - Audio on different browsers\n1541:   - Performance with high cell counts\n1542:   - Accessibility testing\n1543: \n1544: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1545: \n1546: ### 6.5 Documentation (LOW - Knowledge Transfer)\n1547: \n1548: - [x] Write README.md\n1549:   - Project overview\n1550:   - Installation instructions\n1551:   - Controls and gameplay guide\n1552:   - Configuration options\n1553:   - Known issues and limitations\n1554: - [ ] Add code comments\n1555:   - Complex algorithms (movement detection, simulation)\n1556:   - State machine logic\n1557:   - Performance-critical sections\n1558: - [ ] Document API interfaces\n1559:   - Component props\n1560:   - Utility functions\n1561:   - Configuration schemas\n1562:   - Type definitions\n1563: - [ ] Create developer guide\n1564:   - Architecture overview\n1565:   - How to add new features\n1566:   - Debugging tips\n1567:   - Common patterns\n1568: - [ ] Document expert settings\n1569:   - Each parameter explanation\n1570:   - Recommended values\n1571:   - Impact on gameplay\n1572: \n1573: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1574: \n1575: **Implementation Summary (README.md):**\n1576: \n1577: - Created comprehensive README.md with project overview, installation instructions, and gameplay guide\n1578: - Documented all controls including keyboard shortcuts, mouse/touch controls, and mobile gestures\n1579: - Explained game mechanics including phases, Conway's rules, pattern classification, Flux system, and level progression\n1580: - Documented configuration options for basic settings and expert settings (all parameters)\n1581: - Added development section with project structure, available scripts, testing information, and tech stack\n1582: - Included architecture highlights for performance optimizations, state management, and accessibility\n1583: - Listed known issues and limitations with current implementation status\n1584: - Added contributing guidelines, license information, and support resources\n1585: \n1586: **Technical Decisions:**\n1587: \n1588: - Used standard README.md format with badges, sections, and code blocks\n1589: - Comprehensive coverage of all game features and controls\n1590: - Clear installation and setup instructions\n1591: - Detailed explanation of game mechanics and scoring system\n1592: - Complete documentation of expert settings parameters\n1593: - Development section helpful for developers and contributors\n1594: - Markdown formatting with proper headers, tables, and code formatting\n1595: \n1596: **Test Coverage:**\n1597: \n1598: - All existing 364 tests continue to pass\n1599: - README.md verified to be valid markdown\n1600: \n1601: ### 6.6 Code Quality & Refinement (COMPLETED - 2026-02-16)\n1602: \n1603: **Goal**: Fix lint errors, improve code quality, and ensure production readiness\n1604: \n1605: - [x] Fixed lint errors and code quality issues\n1606: - [x] Fixed clearTimeout not being recognized as global (changed to window.clearTimeout)\n1607: - [x] Added missing globals to ESLint config (Blob, URL, FileReader, HTMLInputElement)\n1608: - [x] Created separate vitest.config.ts to fix build error\n1609: - [x] Fixed 'any' types in SettingsPanel component (use Record<string, unknown>)\n1610: - [x] Removed unused error variable in catch block\n1611: - [x] Fixed synchronous setState in effects for FluxDisplay, ScoreDisplay, and Game components\n1612: - [x] Refactored levelStats from state to computed value using useMemo\n1613: - [x] Added eslint rule override to allow 'any' types in test files\n1614: - [x] All verification completed (360 tests passing, build successful, TypeScript clean)\n1615: \n1616: **Implementation Summary:**\n1617: \n1618: - Fixed clearTimeout global recognition issue by using window.clearTimeout throughout codebase\n1619: - Added missing browser globals to ESLint configuration: Blob, URL, FileReader, HTMLInputElement\n1620: - Created vitest.config.ts to separate test configuration from main Vite config, resolving build conflicts\n1621: - Replaced 'any' types in SettingsPanel component with Record<string, unknown> for proper type safety\n1622: - Removed unused error variable from catch block to satisfy ESLint no-unused-vars rule\n1623: - Fixed synchronous setState warnings in React effects:\n1624:   - FluxDisplay: wrapped setState in useCallback with proper dependency tracking\n1625:   - ScoreDisplay: wrapped setState in useCallback with proper dependency tracking\n1626:   - Game: refactored levelStats from state to computed value using useMemo\n1627: - Added eslint rule override for test files to allow 'any' types when needed for test doubles\n1628: \n1629: **Technical Decisions:**\n1630: \n1631: - Used window.clearTimeout to ensure global recognition across all environments\n1632: - Created separate vitest.config.ts to isolate test environment configuration from production build\n1633: - Record<string, unknown> provides better type safety than 'any' while maintaining flexibility\n1634: - useMemo for levelStats prevents unnecessary re-computation and state updates\n1635: - useCallback for setState functions ensures stable references across renders\n1636: - ESLint overrides for test files scoped to .test.ts and .spec.ts extensions only\n1637: \n1638: **Verification Results:**\n1639: \n1640: - All 360 tests passing\n1641: - Build successful (npm run build)\n1642: - TypeScript compilation clean (npm run typecheck)\n1643: - ESLint passing (npm run lint)\n1644: - Git tag 0.1.5 created and pushed\n1645: \n1646: ---\n1647: \n1648: ## Parallel Development Tracks\n1649: \n1650: ### Track A (Can start after Project Setup):\n1651: \n1652: - Type definitions → Shared utilities → All other systems\n1653: \n1654: ### Track B (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1655: \n1656: - Phase Management → UI Overlay → Phase Status Display\n1657: - Canvas Rendering → Grid Interaction\n1658: \n1659: ### Track C (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1660: \n1661: - User Interaction → Audio Sonification → Visual Polish\n1662: - Flux Management → Grid Interaction\n1663: \n1664: ### Track D (Can start after Canvas Rendering + User Interaction + Flux Management):\n1665: \n1666: - Grid Integration → Playable MVP\n1667: \n1668: ### Track E (Can start after MVP):\n1669: \n1670: - Intro Overlay → Main UI Controls → Settings Panel\n1671: - Movement Detection → Scoring System → Level Progression\n1672: \n1673: ### Track F (Can start after Level Progression):\n1674: \n1675: - Transition System → Victory Screen\n1676: \n1677: ### Track G (Can start after Scoring + Level Progression):\n1678: \n1679: - Audio Sonification → Visual Polish → Mobile Enhancements\n1680: \n1681: ### Track H (Can start after all features):\n1682: \n1683: - Expert Settings → Presets → Error Handling → Accessibility → Performance → Testing → Documentation\n1684: \n1685: ---\n1686: \n1687: ## Critical Path (Sequential Must-Haves for MVP):\n1688: \n1689: 1. **Project Setup** → Build system\n1690: 2. **Type Definitions** → All type-safe development\n1691: 3. **Shared Utilities** → Validation and state management\n1692: 4. **Simulation Engine** → Core gameplay logic\n1693: 5. **Phase Management with COUNTDOWN** → Game flow control\n1694: 6. **Canvas Rendering** → Visual feedback\n1695: 7. **User Interaction** → Input handling\n1696: 8. **Flux Management** → Resource system\n1697: 9. **Grid Integration** → Playable MVP\n1698: \n1699: ## Testing Milestones:\n1700: \n1701: - **After Sprint 1**: MVP manually playable (place cells, watch simulation, all phases work)\n1702: - **After Sprint 2**: Full game UI (intro, controls, scoring, settings)\n1703: - **After Sprint 3**: Complete game loop (intro → levels → transitions → victory)\n1704: - **After Sprint 4**: Audio and polish (all sounds, visual enhancements, mobile support)\n1705: - **After Sprint 5**: Expert settings and customization\n1706: - **After Sprint 6**: Production-ready with stability, accessibility, performance, tests, and docs\n1707: \n1708: ## Success Criteria:\n1709: \n1710: - [ ] Playable MVP after Sprint 1 (can place cells and run simulation with all phases)\n1711: - [ ] Complete UI after Sprint 2 (intro, controls, settings)\n1712: - [ ] Full game loop after Sprint 3 (intro → levels → scoring → transitions → victory)\n1713: - [ ] Audio and polish after Sprint 4 (all sounds, animations, mobile support)\n1714: - [ ] All features implemented after Sprint 5 (expert settings, presets)\n1715: - [ ] Production-ready after Sprint 6 (stability, accessibility, performance, tests, docs)\n1716: - [ ] 60fps performance with 500+ cells\n1717: - [ ] Works on mobile and desktop\n1718: - [ ] Audio works across all major browsers\n1719: - [ ] No console errors or warnings in production\n1720: - [ ] High score persistence works\n1721: - [ ] Expert settings properly configure all systems\n1722: - [ ] All critical edge cases handled gracefully\n1723: - [ ] Accessible keyboard navigation\n1724: - [ ] Comprehensive test coverage for core systems\n1725: - [ ] Clear documentation for developers and players\n1726: \n1727: ## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n1728: \n1729: - **Framework**: React/Vite (recommended for performance and DX)\n1730: - **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useReducer, useRef) - minimal, no external library needed\n1731: - **Styling**: CSS modules or vanilla CSS with CSS variables for theming\n1732: - **Testing**: Vitest (fast, compatible with Vite)\n1733: - **Build Tool**: Vite (recommended for speed and simplicity)\n1734: \n1735: ## Implementation Order Recommendations:\n1736: \n1737: ### Week 1: Foundation\n1738: \n1739: 1. Project setup (Day 1)\n1740: 2. Type definitions (Day 1)\n1741: 3. Shared utilities (Day 2)\n1742: 4. Simulation engine (Day 2-3)\n1743: 5. Phase management with COUNTDOWN (Day 3-4)\n1744: 6. Canvas rendering (Day 4)\n1745: \n1746: ### Week 2: Interaction & UI\n1747: \n1748: 7. User interaction (Day 1)\n1749: 8. Flux management (Day 1-2)\n1750: 9. Grid interaction (Day 2) - MVP milestone reached\n1751: 10. Intro overlay (Day 3)\n1752: 11. Main UI controls (Day 3-4)\n1753: 12. Phase status display (Day 4)\n1754: \n1755: ### Week 3: Scoring & Progression\n1756: \n1757: 13. Movement detection (Day 1-2)\n1758: 14. Scoring system (Day 2-3)\n1759: 15. Settings panel (Day 3)\n1760: 16. Level progression (Day 4)\n1761: \n1762: ### Week 4: Transitions & Audio\n1763: \n1764: 17. Transition system (Day 1-2)\n1765: 18. Victory screen (Day 2)\n1766: 19. Audio sonification (Day 3-4)\n1767: 20. Visual polish (Day 4)\n1768: \n1769: ### Week 5: Advanced Features\n1770: \n1771: 21. Expert settings (Day 1-3)\n1772: 22. Mobile enhancements (Day 3)\n1773: 23. Presets system (Day 4)\n1774: \n1775: ### Week 6: Quality Assurance\n1776: \n1777: 24. Error handling (Day 1)\n1778: 25. Accessibility (Day 1-2)\n1779: 26. Performance optimization (Day 2)\n1780: 27. Testing (Day 3-4)\n1781: 28. Documentation (Day 4)\n1782: \n1783: ## Notes:\n1784: \n1785: - Update status (checkmark) as tasks are completed\n1786: - The plan is prioritized: CRITICAL first, then HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW\n1787: - Parallel tracks enable concurrent work where dependencies allow\n1788: - Focus on MVP first, then incrementally add polish\n1789: - src/lib/ is project's standard library for shared utilities\n1790: - Prefer consolidated implementations in src/lib/ over ad-hoc copies\n1791: - Always run lint and typecheck commands after completing features\n1792: - Test on both desktop and mobile throughout development\n1793: - Gather user feedback during development to improve UX\n1794: - Document decisions and trade-offs in comments or docs\n1795: - Keep code modular and maintainable for future enhancements\n1796: \n1797: ## Recent Progress:\n1798: \n1799: **Current Status (2026-02-16):**\n1800: \n1801: - **Sprint 1-5 Complete**: MVP, scoring, levels, transitions, audio, visual polish, mobile, and expert settings fully implemented\n1802: - **Sprint 6 In Progress**: Error Boundary completed, README.md completed, browser compatibility completed, remaining items (accessibility, performance, testing) pending\n1803: - **All 374 tests passing** with comprehensive coverage of implemented features\n1804: - **Production-ready core game** with complete feature set, documentation, and browser compatibility\n1805: \n1806: **Recent Completion:**\n1807: \n1808: - **Sprint 6.1 Error Boundary**: Implemented global error boundary with user-friendly error UI, development-mode error details, and reload functionality. All 4 tests passing.\n1809: - **Sprint 6.5 README.md (v0.1.8)**: Created comprehensive README.md with project overview, installation instructions, controls and gameplay guide, game mechanics explanation, configuration options, development section with project structure and tech stack, architecture highlights, known issues and limitations, and contributing guidelines.\n1810: - **Sprint 6.1 Browser Compatibility & Edge Cases (v0.1.9)**: Created centralized feature detection module, enhanced localStorage handling with quota support and validation, integrated feature detection on app initialization, added comprehensive test coverage (10 tests), all 374 tests passing.\n1811: \n1812: ---\n1813: \n1814: **Documentation Update (2026-02-16):**\n1815: \n1816: - Updated IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md to mark Error Boundary as complete (Sprint 6.1, lines 1300-1303)\n1817: - Cleaned up Recent Progress section by removing outdated turn summaries\n1818: - Consolidated progress notes for better readability and maintainability\n1819: - Documentation now reflects current implementation state accurately\n1820: \n1821: ---\n1822: \n1823: **Turn Summary (2026-02-16):**\n1824: \n1825: - **Error Boundary (v0.0.1)**: Implemented global error boundary in Sprint 6.1 with user-friendly error UI, development-mode error details, reload functionality, and 4 tests passing\n1826: - **Reduced Motion Support (v0.0.2)**: Implemented accessibility support in Sprint 6.2 by adding prefers-reduced-motion media queries to all 10 CSS files, disabling 76 animation/transition instances for users with motion sensitivity\n1827: \n\n(End of file - total 1827 lines)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"- Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n- Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n- All 341 tests passing\n\n**Technical Decisions:**\n\n- Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n- Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n- Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n- Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n- Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n- Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n- Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n\n- All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n- Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n- Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771234151284,"end":1771234151288}}}}
